; Exercise 09-options (chapter 9).
;
; A command takes these arguments, in any order:
;   --verbose          sets :verbose to #true
;   --limit N          sets :limit to the Integer N
;   anything else      a file name, added to :files in order
; With no option, :verbose is #false and :limit is 10.
;
;   (parse-options '("a.txt" "--limit" "3" "b.txt"))
;   is (:ok {:verbose #false :limit 3 :files ("a.txt" "b.txt")})
;
; The failures:
;   (:error "--limit needs a number")     --limit at the end
;   (:error "not a number" text)          --limit followed by a non-Integer
;   (:error "no files")                   no file name at all
;
; A program would call it as (parse-options (program-arguments!)).
; Then run: tutorial/check.sh 09-options

(import result)   ; ok, failure
(import list)     ; reverse

